I had stars in my eyes

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.930
and it's so small.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:07.670
Did you know that stealing
mail is a federal crime, Kelly?

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:08.790
- I did actually.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.720
- Well, I didn't know that
until somebody started

00:04:11.720 --> 00:04:14.470
stealing mail in our town and
they were like on the case.

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:15.840
Like who's stealing all the mail.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:19.890
The culprit was, they
found out it was a pet crow

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:21.620
that a woman had named Poe the Crow

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:24.140
who was flying around,
stealing all the mail.

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:26.300
Just because you're a
bird, it doesn't mean you

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.820
can't get arrested.

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:31.870
They put crow on house arrest
and he became an indoor crow

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.330
for the rest of his life.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:35.900
- The craziest part is
that if actually she

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:37.980
trained the crow to do that.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.430
That's the deeper story there.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:40.900
- She's like, fly over to the marine house

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:42.700
and see what kind of mail they're getting.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:44.430
- See if anyone got
any cash for Christmas.

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:47.940
- If she did, that would make
me even love it even more.

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:49.976
- I know you're like, free the crow.

00:04:49.976 --> 00:04:51.410
- Free the crow, you guys.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:53.880
- You kept it like
daytime with your mouth.

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:56.333
- I did, I did, I really did.

00:04:56.333 --> 00:04:59.250
- So how did your family
end up in a Little Compton

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.396
'cause they weren't
originally from there, right?

00:05:01.396 --> 00:05:02.679
- No, they were from New York city,

00:05:02.679 --> 00:05:04.256
so it was sort of a
strange place to end up.

00:05:04.256 --> 00:05:05.630
But my parents, they met at work.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:06.963
There they are.

00:05:06.963 --> 00:05:08.470
They're recreating the
"American Gothic" photo.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:10.150
So my dad looked like John Belushi.

00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:11.810
- [Kelly] I totally see
where you get your humor.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:13.080
I love your family.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.187
- When they decided to
have kids my dad said,

00:05:15.187 --> 00:05:16.937
"I'll do it in one of two places,

00:05:16.937 --> 00:05:20.202
"Manhattan or this tiny town called

00:05:20.202 --> 00:05:21.512
Little Compton, Rhode Island"

00:05:21.512 --> 00:05:22.810
and my mom picked the road less traveled

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:24.780
and that's where the book starts.

00:05:24.780 --> 00:05:26.130
- Oh my God, I love this.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.010
It's like a movie.

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:28.780
- It's like a movie, but it was fun.

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:30.880
I mean, it was this quirky
household that I grew up in.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:33.736
- I love, the photo says it all.

00:05:33.736 --> 00:05:35.420
I grew up in a small town as well.

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:37.500
Like what was the biggest
challenge for you?

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.260
- I mean, I don't know
if you guys tend to,

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:42.560
I have so much hair, like
the "Mad TV" hair department

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:44.276
said I could wig a village.

00:05:44.276 --> 00:05:45.590
(laughing)

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:47.960
So, and `we only had a general store,

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:49.520
we didn't even have a grocery store

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:51.260
so they didn't even have hair conditioner.

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:53.252
It was just like cream rinse, you know.

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:54.085
Look at that, look at that.

00:05:54.085 --> 00:05:54.918
Look at that hair, look at me.

00:05:54.918 --> 00:05:55.930
I was a ginger.

00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:57.806
I was like a helmet.

00:05:57.806 --> 00:05:58.990
- Oh my god.
- Look at how confident.

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:01.750
Look at the size of my head
versus that other little girl,

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:04.437
like, look how calm , I
was so the alpha in that.

00:06:04.437 --> 00:06:05.890
- [Kelly] Well first of
all, you're in front of her,

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:07.140
so she's in the back, yeah.

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:09.635
- She's in front but like-
- You're in the foreground.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:10.710
- But so I couldn't be, so my mom-

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:11.800
- I'm gonna be honest with you,

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:14.410
that might be one of my favorite haircuts

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:15.739
I've ever seen on a kid (laughs).

00:06:15.739 --> 00:06:17.865
- Look how confident,
look at my pants, like,

00:06:17.865 --> 00:06:20.430
look at the, like, am I still in a diaper?

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:21.750
What's happening with the pleats?

00:06:21.750 --> 00:06:23.119
- [Kelly] It's awesome.

00:06:23.119 --> 00:06:25.243
- So, my mom, there was only
on place to get your hair cut

00:06:25.243 --> 00:06:26.076
in town and it was at Jimmy the Barber

00:06:26.076 --> 00:06:27.900
who cut the cops and
the lobstermens' hair.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:30.690
So I would get the boys,
like helmet or like buzz cut.

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:32.420
And I looked like Barb
