00:06:56.773 --> 00:06:59.540
We can't wait to do this book with you.

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:01.780
I sold it on the way to her funeral.

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:03.070
I had literally been trying for years

00:07:03.070 --> 00:07:05.117
and she was barely in the proposal.

00:07:05.117 --> 00:07:07.279
And then like now I felt
like it was her book

00:07:07.279 --> 00:07:10.360
and my friend read it and she
goes, it's not your memoir,

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.040
it's your mom-oir.

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:15.060
And she was so funny and
I feel like I gave her

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:18.340
this funny book that sort of honoring

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:20.330
everything that she gave
to my brother and I.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.520
- Yeah,
(audience applause)

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:22.530
and wow, you're an optimistic.

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:24.668
Like, to turn that around, that's amazing.

00:07:24.668 --> 00:07:26.380
- Yeah, oh my God.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:29.220
- Well Arden's book is called
"Little Miss Little Compton".

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:30.727
Y'all got to go buy it.

